Hy-Nomas Local Studio and native ComfyUI integration — By T8star

This local distribution contains a GPL-3.0 derivative of
PedroMarinhoDev/ComfyUI-Hy-Nomas, pinned in versions.json. The upstream
LICENSE and NOTICE are preserved in custom_nodes/ComfyUI-HyNomas-T8.
Tencent Hy-Nomas source notices and the Apache-2.0 license remain in
that package's docs/upstream directory.

T8 additions (2026): local Chinese UI with pink/white branding; in-process
inference orchestration; portable Windows launchers; custom model paths;
verified resumable downloads; explicit history budgets and cleanup;
transactional continuation; bounded-memory MP4 export and diagnostics.

ComfyUI, CPython, uv, PyTorch, Triton and their dependencies retain their
own licenses and notices. Their source/version information is recorded
in versions.json and the installed package metadata. Existing license
files within the bundled runtimes must be retained when redistributing.

Bundled ComfyUI host change (2026-10-28): release temporary cache-probe
references after collecting cached node IDs, so RAM-pressure eviction can
release unused cached models during repeated prompts. The upstream source
commit remains recorded in versions.json; this local change is covered by
tests/test_executor_cache_lifetime.py. Standalone-node users can apply the
included patches/comfyui-cache-lifetime.patch to the matching ComfyUI host.

Model weights are downloaded separately. PixelUMM model weights and
derivatives are labeled NVIDIA One-Way Noncommercial License by NVIDIA;
research/evaluation only. Do not apply this code distribution's GPL-3.0
or Tencent's source-code Apache-2.0 license to every model weight.
See models.manifest.json and the original model cards:
https://huggingface.co/tencent/Hy-Nomas
https://huggingface.co/nvidia/PixelUMM
https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Qwen-Image_ComfyUI

This package is a T8 derivative and is not represented as an official
Tencent, NVIDIA, Comfy-Org or PedroMarinhoDev release.

T8star program distribution 0.2.1 adds a PowerShell launch-time updater, verified program manifests, backups and rollback. Inference sources retain their previously tested bytes. ComfyUI sources include the documented cache-reference fix; Python/site-packages and model weights are not distributed in the program ZIP.
